
== 0. Input ====================================================
  46_line_level_data.csv: 741 lines

== 1. Mann-Whitney p-value floors ==============================
  Both are computed, not asserted. n1 = 56 melanoma, n2 = 940 others.

  NORMAL APPROXIMATION
    sigma_U = 2091.3 | max |z| = 12.585
    floor on the two-sided p  ~ 1e-35.6
    This is the bound that applies to the tests actually reported,
    because those use the normal approximation with tie correction.

  EXACT TEST
    number of distinct group assignments: choose(996, 56) = 1e92.4
    floor on the two-sided p  = 2 / choose(N, n1) ~ 1e-92.1
    The exact floor is about 1e56 times smaller than the normal one.

  WHAT THIS CORRECTS: script 48 described ~1e-36 as the smallest
  attainable p for this comparison. That holds for the normal
  approximation only. The exact test can in principle go far lower. No
  reported value changes: the two significant comparisons are 8.7e-17 and
  1.1e-16, far above both floors, and the exact test is not used here
  because with n = 996 it is computationally impractical and the normal
  approximation is the standard choice at this sample size.

