== 3. Nested models refitted on identical lines =================
  Script 46 fitted M0 and M1 on 736 lines and M2 and M3 on 611, because
  copy number is missing for some. A percentage retained computed across
  models fitted on different samples confounds adjustment with sample
  change. All four models are refitted here on the complete-case set.

  RASSF9: lines with methylation + expression + lineage = 736
         of those with usable copy number (complete case) = 611

    model                                n       beta                 95% CI           p  retained
    M0 unadjusted                      611     -1.456  [-1.749, -1.163]    6.56e-21      100%
    M1 + lineage                       611     -1.241  [-1.560, -0.923]    8.66e-14       85%
    M2 + log2 copy number              611     -1.456  [-1.749, -1.164]    5.19e-21      100%
    M3 + lineage + log2 copy number    611     -1.234  [-1.551, -0.917]    9.91e-14       85%
    all four models fitted on the same 611 lines
    for reference, M0 on all 736 lines: beta = -1.384, p = 2.56e-24
    (a difference between this and M0 above reflects the restriction to
     lines with copy number, not any adjustment)

  RASSF10: lines with methylation + expression + lineage = 736
         of those with usable copy number (complete case) = 611

    model                                n       beta                 95% CI           p  retained
    M0 unadjusted                      611     -1.443  [-1.709, -1.177]    2.75e-24      100%
    M1 + lineage                       611     -1.340  [-1.623, -1.058]    2.67e-19       93%
    M2 + log2 copy number              611     -1.368  [-1.631, -1.105]    1.23e-22       95%
    M3 + lineage + log2 copy number    611     -1.278  [-1.556, -1.000]    2.71e-18       89%
    all four models fitted on the same 611 lines
    for reference, M0 on all 736 lines: beta = -1.485, p = 1.96e-31
    (a difference between this and M0 above reflects the restriction to
     lines with copy number, not any adjustment)

== 4. Changes required in the analysis note =====================
  1. Methods: attribute the ~1e-36 floor to the NORMAL APPROXIMATION and
     state the exact-test floor separately, with the reason the normal
     approximation is used at this sample size.
  2. Table 8: replace with the four models above, all on the same lines,
     and report the all-lines M0 separately for reference.
  3. Table 2 or Results 1: add the subtype breakdown of the 39 paired
     lines from section 2.
  4. Throughout: methylation-ASSOCIATED repression, not demonstrated
     silencing; and state that whether promoter methylation constrains UV
     inducibility is untested here.
